From 9186d70126cd8b62ad50b1f744fe7adf8cb498e3 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sat, 24 Oct 2026 10:09:33 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] Add firmware OTA: install a Realtek firmware tar(.gz) into
 the other A/B slot

ota.sh gets fw_check / fw_apply [stage|next|default|once|keep] / fw_status / fw_log, driven
by a firmware.txt manifest (model-pinned, sha256-verified, URL pinned to this repo) and
written through the existing www2/sh/fwboot.sh, so every flash-safety rule stays in
one place. Never automatic: cron only notifies, once per version.

- fw_apply next (preselected): write the slot and arm a trial boot that is kept if it
  comes up cleanly (fwboot.sh bootonce N 1), but DO NOT reboot. The device tries the new
  slot at its next restart (power cut, crash, manual), fw_loaded.sh makes it the default
  if it starts cleanly, and U-Boot's watchdog falls back to the current slot if not.
- fw_apply default: write the slot and make it the default boot slot (fwboot.sh
  setdefault), no reboot, no automatic fall-back. Only once/keep reboot, as before.
- fw_check reports "pending":true once the firmware is written and set to boot at the
  next restart; the page shows "Waiting for restart" and cron stops notifying
- fwboot.sh: accept .tar.gz (magic-byte detection, unpacked once in place, capped at
  64 MiB); new `info` command reporting the one flashable slot and why not
- ota.cgi / ota.html: Firmware card on Software Update (check, five install modes,
  progress, reboot wait); fwupload/bootpart pages accept .tar.gz
- fwpublish.sh: builds firmware.txt from a fwu tar and prints the release steps
- FIRMWARE_OTA.md: how it works and what is and is not tested

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
