new file mode 100644
index 0000000..10147d3
--- /dev/null
+++ b/FIRMWARE_OTA.md
@@ -0,0 +1,89 @@
+# Firmware OTA (Realtek Luna firmware → the other flash slot)
+
+The normal OTA (`ota.sh check` / `apply`) only swaps app files under `/lmepisowifi`. This is
+the other half: it installs a **vendor-format firmware tar** (`uImage` + `rootfs` + `md5.txt` +
+`fwu.sh` + `fwu_ver`, as `.tar` or `.tar.gz`) into the **inactive A/B flash slot**.
+
+Admin page: **Software Update → Firmware (other slot)**. It is never automatic. Cron only sends
+a notification (once per version) that a firmware is waiting.
+
+## Publishing a firmware (on your computer)
+
+```sh
+./fwpublish.sh path/to/PGN6401V_fwu_img.tar PGN6401V fw-v8.1.2 "what changed"
+```
+
+It checks the tar against its own `md5.txt`, gzips it if needed, and writes `firmware.txt`
+(version, model, URL, sha256, size). Then it prints the three steps left:
+
+1. attach the `.tar.gz` to a GitHub Release with that tag,
+2. commit and push `firmware.txt` to `main`,
+3. purge jsDelivr's cached copy so devices see it now:
+   `curl -sL https://purge.jsdelivr.net/gh/OWNER/REPO@main/firmware.txt`
+
+`firmware.txt` fields: `fw_version`, `fw_model`, `fw_url`, `fw_sha256`, optional `fw_size`,
+`fw_notes`, `fw_url_mirror`.
+
+**Give every build a new `fwu_ver` string.** `fw_version` is the tar's own `fwu_ver` (the part
+before ` -- `), and the device decides "is there an update?" by comparing it with the version it
+is running. The vendor `fwu.sh` refuses an equal version for the same reason.
+
+## What the device does
+
+| Step | Rule |
+|---|---|
+| Manifest | `firmware.txt` must carry `fw_model` equal to `FW_MODEL` in this repo's `ota.sh`, a 64-hex sha256, and a URL inside this repo's Releases (or its jsDelivr tree). Anything else is refused. |
+| Slot | Only the slot that is **neither running nor the default**. If there is none (for example a trial boot is pending) it says why and writes nothing. |
+| Download | To RAM (`/tmp/ota`), sha256 checked against the manifest. A mismatch deletes it. |
+| Write | `www2/sh/fwboot.sh flash`: re-checks `md5.txt`, sizes against the slot's UBI volumes, writes `uImage` then `rootfs`, reads both back, and only then records the slot's version. An interrupted write leaves the slot marked empty. |
+| RAM | A `.tar.gz` is unpacked once; peak is about twice its size, plus the `rootfs` while writing. Limit 64 MiB. |
+
+After writing you pick one of five options. Only the last two reboot the device; the first three
+never do, so nobody is interrupted.
+
+- **Just write it**: nothing else changes; boot it later from *Boot Partitions*.
+- **Write it and try it at the next restart** (preselected): arms the same trial boot as the
+  last option (`fwboot.sh bootonce N 1`) but does not reboot. The device keeps running as it is. The
+  next time it restarts for any reason (power cut, crash, manual reboot) it boots the new slot once.
+  If that comes up cleanly `fw_loaded.sh` keeps it as the default; if it hangs, U-Boot's watchdog
+  drops back to the current slot. Cancel it before then with *Boot Partitions*.
+- **Write it and make it the default boot slot**: runs `fwboot.sh setdefault` on the
+  new slot and stops. The device keeps running as it is and comes up on the new firmware the next
+  time it restarts for any reason (power cut, crash, manual reboot). This is a plain default
+  switch, not a trial boot: nothing is set up to fall back automatically if the new firmware fails
+  to start. To undo it, make the old slot the default again on *Boot Partitions*.
+- **Reboot into it once to test**: reboots now; the reboot after that returns to the current
+  firmware unless you make the new one the default.
+- **Reboot into it and keep it if it starts cleanly**: reboots now; becomes the default once
+  `fw_loaded.sh` runs at the end of a good boot. If it never gets there, U-Boot's watchdog falls
+  back to the old slot.
+
+Once a firmware is written and set to boot at the next restart, `fw_check` reports it as
+`"pending":true` (with `pending_slot`) and the page shows *Waiting for restart* instead of offering
+it again. Cron does not nag about it.
+
+`/lmepisowifi` is its own UBIFS volume, so vouchers, income and settings are in neither slot.
+
+`.tar.gz` also works on **Firmware Upload** and **Boot Partitions → download from URL**.
+
+## Command line (on the device)
+
+```sh
+sh /lmepisowifi/ota.sh fw_check              # JSON: running / latest / target slot
+sh /lmepisowifi/ota.sh fw_apply stage|next|default|once|keep   # only once/keep reboot
+sh /lmepisowifi/ota.sh fw_status             # JSON: status + message
+sh /lmepisowifi/ota.sh fw_log
+sh /lmepisowifi/www2/sh/fwboot.sh info       # slots, versions, which slot is flashable
+```
+
+## What has and has not been tested
+
+Tested with stand-ins for `nv`, `ubinfo`, `ubiupdatevol`, `/proc/mtd`, `wget` and `reboot`, under
+`dash`, using a real `fwu` tar: manifest checks, model mismatch, checksum mismatch, gzip
+unpacking (including corrupt and oversized input), slot selection, every install mode, flash
+failure, locking, stale status, and the admin page in a headless browser.
+
+**Not tested on a device:** BusyBox `ash`/applet behaviour, the real U-Boot `sw_tryactive`
+fallback and `fw_loaded.sh` commit behaviour (this relies on what the comments in `fwboot.sh`
+say they do), and free RAM on the target. Try **Just write it**, then **Boot it once to test**,
+before relying on **keep**.
